{
  "feature": "Admin E2-B: Event edit lineup chips (matched, unsure, typed) and Add an artist",
  "note": "Boards: design_handoff_admin_redesign/boards/06-events-artists-prices/event-edit (desktop) and event-edit-mobile (phone; the phone chips carry Add a show's arrow and x by orchestrator ruling); B+ addendum 5 04/past-show-d for the same field on a played show. CONTACT_SHEET_ROLE=admin. Read-only: types into Add an artist but never presses Save; no scratch-DB writes. Each row stubs GET /v1/admin/events/:id with a bill of a matched headliner, an unsure support (match_status ambiguous) and a typed name with no artist. CAVEAT, as admin-a7-tour-name-sold-out notes: the editor reads that GET on the SERVER (page.tsx apiClient.get), which a browser `route` cannot answer, so the cells show the fixture event's real bill unless the shooter serves this payload to the server render. The artist search (`/v1/admin/artists?...`) runs in the browser, so its stub does apply. By hand: Delete on a focused chip removes it, Alt+arrow moves it, and a failed Save (stop the API) snaps the bill back with 'The lineup is as it was.'",
